ved from Disco, circa 1981, that combines dance beats with a pop/R'n'B song structure. Because there is such an emphasis on fully-formed songs in dance-pop, it's often viewed as a separate classification unto itself apart from pure dance. Dance-pop is also closely related to the teen pop and Eurodance movements in the mid-1980s and late 1990s, the rise of boy bands and girl groups, and the reintroduction of the vocoder and similar such innovations.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Justin Bieber", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "PinkPantheress", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sabrina Carpenter", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electronic": {"genre": "electronic", "country_code": "eg", "country_name": "Egypt", "summary": "Electronic music refers to music that emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beach 