stic body moves, are an important feature.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daniel Caesar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jeff Buckley", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kali Uchis", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "PARTYNEXTDOOR", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "SZA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sade", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "synth-pop": {"genre": "synth-pop", "country_code": "eg", "country_name": "Egypt", "summary": "Synth Pop was one of the most distinctive subgenres of new wave. In the early '80s, a number of bands primarily British and heavily influenced Roxy Music and David Bowie adapted the electronic innovations of bands like Kraftwerk for pop songs. Initially, in the hands of artists like Gary Numan, The Human League and Depeche Mode, the sound was eerie, sterile, and vaguely menacing, since the electronics droned on relentlessly without any change in inflections.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Harry Styles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Mar\u00edas", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "T